      "details": [
        {
          "label": "STRIDE",
          "text": "Tampering, Repudiation, Information disclosure, Elevation of privilege"
        },
        {
          "label": "Threat",
          "text": "Someone other than the ISMS manager reads internal findings and risk decisions, or a record is changed so that a control looks verified, a risk accepted or a finding closed without the documented steps (ADR-016)."
        },
        {
          "label": "Attack scenario",
          "text": "An ordinary account calls the ISMS routes; a client sends a status field or a decision through the record route; a stale browser overwrites a newer record; a verification is recorded on stale evidence; attached output smuggles a credential into the records; an \"internal audit\" is recorded as independent by its own planner; an activity row is edited afterwards."
        },
        {
          "label": "Security controls",
          "text": "PA-06 to PA-08 behind the platform administrator gate (PLATFORM_ADMIN with MFA; 404 for everyone else) and a step-up for every decision; strict schemas with no status field; server-side state machines with documented conditions; optimistic concurrency; serialized writes; the freshness rule checked by the server; attachments limited in size and refused when they contain secret material; database CHECKs, a guard trigger and an append-only activity table with SELECT and INSERT only."
        },
        {
          "label": "Residual risk",
          "text": "A platform administrator can record any decision (L-82); the activity history is not tamper-evident (L-81)."
        },
        {
          "label": "Testing strategy",
          "text": "tests/isms/isms.test.ts (authorization, step-up, every condition, conflicts, malformed input, secrets, database guards), packages/shared/src/isms.test.ts, negative controls NC-22-01 to NC-22-05, tests/e2e/isms.spec.ts in three engines."
        }
      ]
